# WebSocket Real-time Notifications

Connect to WebSocket for real-time lead notifications:

## Connection URL
```
wss://your-domain.com/ws/leads?token={{JWT_TOKEN}}&user_id={{USER_ID}}
```

## Event Types

### 1. New Lead Event
```json
{
  "event": "new_lead",
  "data": {
    "lead_id": "uuid",
    "user_id": "user123",
    "lead_form_id": "form456",
    "source": {
      "platform": "twitter",
      "post_url": "https://twitter.com/user/status/123",
      "post_content": "Looking for CRM...",
      "author_name": "John Doe",
      "author_handle": "@johndoe",
      "matched_keywords": ["CRM"],
      "matched_signals": ["budget approved"]
    },
    "ai_suggested_reply": "Hi John! I saw you're looking for...",
    "score": 0.85,
    "created_at": "2025-10-13T10:30:00Z"
  }
}
```

### 2. Lead Updated Event
```json
{
  "event": "lead_updated",
  "data": {
    "lead_id": "uuid",
    "status": "contacted",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-13T11:00:00Z"
  }
}
```

### 3. Monitoring Status Event
```json
{
  "event": "monitoring_status",
  "data": {
    "lead_form_id": "form456",
    "status": "active",
    "platforms": ["twitter", "linkedin"],
    "leads_today": 12
  }
}
```

## JavaScript Example
```javascript
const ws = new WebSocket(`wss://your-domain.com/ws/leads?token=${token}&user_id=${userId}`);

ws.onopen = () => {
  console.log('Connected to real-time lead notifications');
};

ws.onmessage = (event) => {
  const message = JSON.parse(event.data);

  if (message.event === 'new_lead') {
    // Handle new lead
    console.log('New lead detected:', message.data);
    // Update UI, play notification sound, etc.
  }
};

ws.onerror = (error) => {
  console.error('WebSocket error:', error);
};

ws.onclose = () => {
  console.log('Disconnected from notifications');
};
```

## Testing with wscat
```bash
npm install -g wscat
wscat -c "wss://your-domain.com/ws/leads?token=YOUR_TOKEN&user_id=YOUR_USER_ID"
```

